WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.500
NARRATOR: Thousands
of feet higher up,

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:06.306
in an altogether
different type of forest,

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:10.176
there lives another
very special creature

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.980
that is also unique to China.

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:15.949
The golden snub-nosed
monkey only

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:20.220
lives here in the high mountain
forests of central China.

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:24.157
[music playing]

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:28.828
Up to 13,000 feet
above sea level,

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:33.066
this is the world's largest
high-altitude forest,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.135
where there are
more tree species

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.505
than in any other
deciduous forest on earth.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:46.413
It's spring, and these monkeys
are making the most of it.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.529
This troop has five families.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:08.835
Each family has one
male and several females

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:09.636
with their young.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.809
Males that don't belong
to these families

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:18.812
hang out together in a
monkey bachelor gang.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:27.821
They're an unruly bunch, but for
now, the focus is not on them.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:34.861
It's on the latest
addition to the family,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.930
a brand-new baby girl.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.336
She happens to be the
first born this spring.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:51.377
So all the females in
the family want a cuddle.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:01:59.486
This auntie is first.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.465
Then auntie number
two wants a hold.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:29.716
And auntie number three.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.396
Enough.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:49.135
It's Mom time,
meaning lunch time.

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:01.748
In fact, all the
monkeys want lunch.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:10.156
At this time of year, they spend
a quarter of daylight hours

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.158
eating the fresh, new leaves.

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:20.233
A good source of protein
and their favorite food.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:31.277
As temperatures
rise, the monkeys

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:36.015
follow the leaves as they
spring to life further

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:39.419
and further up the mountain.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:40.486
But eventually the
trees stop growing.

